# Django Testing — pytest-django (Django 6.x)

## Configuração por projecto

Cada projecto é independente. Criar na raiz do projecto:

```ini
# mysite/pytest.ini
[pytest]
DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE = mysite.settings
python_files = tests.py tests_*.py *_tests.py
```

```ini
# educa/pytest.ini  (settings múltiplos)
[pytest]
DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE = educa.settings.local
```

## Marcadores e acesso à BD

```python
@pytest.mark.django_db                  # obrigatório para qualquer acesso à BD
def test_post_count():
    assert Post.objects.count() == 0

@pytest.mark.django_db
class TestPostModel:
    def test_str(self, published_post):
        assert str(published_post) == published_post.title
```

## Fixtures base (conftest.py)

```python
@pytest.fixture
def user(db):
    return get_user_model().objects.create_user(
        username='testuser', email='test@example.com', password='testpass123')

@pytest.fixture
def published_post(db, user):
    return Post.objects.create(
        title='Test Post', slug='test-post', author=user,
        body='body', status=Post.Status.PUBLISHED)
```

### Fixtures django-parler (myshop)

```python
@pytest.fixture
def product(db, category):
    p = Product(category=category, price='9.99', available=True)
    p.set_current_language('en')   # obrigatório antes de atribuir campos traduzidos
    p.name = 'Test Product'
    p.slug = 'test-product'
    p.save()
    return p
```

## Testar views

```python
@pytest.mark.django_db
class TestPostListView:

    def test_returns_200(self, client):
        assert client.get(reverse('blog:post_list')).status_code == 200

    def test_only_published(self, client, published_post, draft_post):
        response = client.get(reverse('blog:post_list'))
        assert published_post in response.context['posts']
        assert draft_post not in response.context['posts']

    def test_redirects_anonymous(self, client):
        response = client.get(reverse('account:dashboard'))
        assert response.status_code == 302

    def test_ok_authenticated(self, client, user):
        client.force_login(user)          # force_login é mais rápido que login()
        assert client.get(reverse('account:dashboard')).status_code == 200
```

## Testar views AJAX

```python
@pytest.mark.django_db
class TestBookmarkAjax:

    def test_requires_post(self, client, user):
        client.force_login(user)
        assert client.get(reverse('blog:post_bookmark', args=[1])).status_code == 405

    def test_requires_login(self, client):
        assert client.post(reverse('blog:post_bookmark', args=[1])).status_code == 302

    def test_returns_json_state(self, client, user, published_post):
        client.force_login(user)
        response = client.post(reverse('blog:post_bookmark', args=[published_post.id]))
        assert response.status_code == 200
        data = json.loads(response.content)
        assert 'bookmarked' in data
        assert 'count' in data
```

## Mock de serviços externos

### Redis

```python
def test_detail_sem_redis(client, product):
    with patch('shop.views.Recommender') as mock_rec:
        mock_rec.side_effect = Exception('Connection refused')
        response = client.get(reverse('shop:product_detail', args=[product.id, product.slug]))
        assert response.status_code == 200
        assert response.context['recommended_products'] == []
```

### Celery

```python
# settings de teste — executar tasks inline sem broker
CELERY_TASK_ALWAYS_EAGER = True

# ou via mock
def test_order_task_called(client, form_data):
    with patch('orders.views.order_created') as mock_task:
        client.post(reverse('orders:order_create'), form_data)
        mock_task.delay.assert_called_once()
```

## Comandos

```bash
pytest                                          # todos os testes
pytest blog/tests.py -v                         # ficheiro específico
pytest blog/tests.py::TestPostModel::test_str   # teste específico
pytest -x                                       # parar ao primeiro erro
pytest -s                                       # mostrar print()
```

## Regras

- `@pytest.mark.django_db` obrigatório em qualquer teste que aceda à BD
- `client.force_login(user)` em vez de `client.login()` — não autentica password
- `set_current_language('en')` antes de atribuir campos parler em fixtures
- Não misturar `django.test.TestCase` com fixtures pytest — incompatíveis
- Redis e Celery sempre em mock nos testes unitários
- Cada teste cria os próprios dados — nunca partilhar estado mutável entre testes
